FulfillRedeemIntegrationConcreteTest
├── when the caller is unauthorized
│   └── it should revert
├── when shares is zero
│   └── it should revert
├── when the receiver has no pending request
│   └── it should revert
├── when shares exceeds the pending entry
│   └── it should revert
├── given the vault is paused
│   └── it should revert
├── when the caller is an authorized operator
│   └── it should settle the request
├── when fulfilled whole at the request price
│   ├── it should burn the escrowed shares
│   ├── it should pay the reserved gross
│   ├── it should zero the pending entry
│   └── it should release the reserved amount from totalPendingAssets
├── when fulfilled partially at the request price
│   ├── it should release the reserved amount proportionally
│   ├── it should leave the remainder pending
│   └── it should settle the remainder exactly on the final fulfilment
├── when the price dropped and fulfilled at the current price
│   ├── it should pay the shares at the current oracle price
│   └── it should release the full reservation
├── when the price rose and fulfilled at the current price
│   └── it should revert
├── when the price is unchanged and fulfilled partially at the current price
│   └── it should pay the pro-rata value without tripping the guard
├── when fulfilled at the current price with a fee
│   ├── it should pay the receiver net of the fee
│   └── it should pay the fee to the fee recipient
├── when a third party inflated the entry
│   └── it should settle the legitimate portion and leave the dust pending
├── when two requests accumulated on the receiver
│   └── it should settle the combined entry whole
├── when the oracle price is zero
│   ├── it should settle at the request price without reading the oracle
│   └── it should refuse the current price
└── when the vault has insufficient asset balance
    └── it should revert
